Z||000009||bHooper||12-26-2000||09:48 PM||||Bob Englert and I took our Gt's out for a run, today... but, unfortunately, the wiggle is still there, comes and goes.  <P>Bob, drove the car, too, and felt it some.<P>we were wondering, if i upgraded everything, as i did... would the rear swaybar cause this feeling?<P>i seem to remember not having a wiggle at all, until i mounted the rear swaybar, back in september.  it's a FOCOA one, that i bought in '94, that had been on my car until i put the tranny in it last spring.<P>i know i still need to do the tranny/engine mounts, but Bob and i thought this to be a possible cause.<P>it's almost like the car is oversteering... ex: i took a 35 mph curve at 55 and had the rear start to come around a bit. (Bob took the same corner in his 85 SE at the same speed... easily)<P>also, it's possible, that the whole thing gets magnified with the camber set at -1 degree at all 4 corners... real twitchy!<P>thanks!<BR>hoop<p>[This message has been edited by bHooper (edited 12-26-2000).]||||reg||2
