Z||000026||william_thorniii||01-12-2001||08:50 AM||||hoop,<P>I do not know how much should be required to spin the nut.  The entire strut is turning though.  This is precisely why they are soooooo hard to remove on older cars.  <P>That bolt carries a near vertical load.  It should not require much torque to seat.  <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||1
Z||000027||bHooper||01-12-2001||08:57 AM||||it appears that i have found <B>SUCCESS</B> in my search to end the stange wiggle!!<P>replacing the tranny mount (and making sure it is secured to the tranny) and the engine mount, appear's to have made the difference!<P>of course, i have only driven the car 11 miles.  but this is the same route that i normally notice the "feeling" on.<P>as for the struts... when i installed them, i had torqued them with the impact whrench.<P>at the moment, i am very happy with the results... best $21 i have spent, yet!<P>i do know that anything else that i am feeling is coming from the tires. at least that is manageable/tolerable.<P>Thanks!<P><P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT<BR>KYB's, Eibach's,<BR>Poly Bushings||||reg||6
